   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing by hand and has not been run through a parser. Several details are uncertain, as noted below.\n\n**Macrocycle**\n- It starts with an N-acetyl penicillamine (Pen), bearing a C(CH3)2 group on sulfur.\n- The ring runs through Asn, Thr, 7-methyl-Trp and N-\u03b5-acetyl-Lys.\n- It closes through a second Pen, joined to the first by an S\u2013S bridge.\n\n**Chain after the ring**\n- Tyr with a 4-(2-aminoethoxy) group on the ring\n- 2-naphthyl-Ala\n- 4-amino-tetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid residue\n- Glu (free CO2H side chain)\n- Asn\n- 3-pyridyl-Ala\n- N-methylglycine\n- Lys, with a C-terminal primary amide\n\n**Lys side-chain lipid tail**\nThe Lys side-chain NH carries two repeats of an amide-linked \u2013C(=O)CH2OCH2CH2OCH2CH2NH\u2013 (OEG) unit. After these comes \u03b3-Glu (free \u03b1-CO2H), then N-methylglycine acylated with a straight-chain fatty acyl group.\n\n**Uncertainties**\n- The fatty acyl chain length is the least certain part. From the pixel spacing I counted a carbonyl plus 13 CH2/CH3 carbons, which gives myristoyl (C14). The count could be off by one carbon.\n- Stereochemistry follows L-amino acids wherever the drawing shows wedges or hashes. Where the wedges are ambiguous (the two Pen centres), I assumed L.\n- The naphthyl-Ala and the tetrahydropyran carbon have plain bonds in the drawing, so they carry no stereo.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)NC(Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)O)C(N)=O)C(C)(C)SSC1(C)C"
